        "title": "Document and cover the additional arithmetic-overflow rejection",
        "path": "packages/metadata-hardening/src/btc.ts",
        "line": 71,
        "evidence_kind": "static source reasoning; not executed",
        "description": "The added finite-result guard runs before finite cap fallback. With rate=1, step=Number.MIN_VALUE, minRate=1 and cap=2, division can overflow even though supplied parameters are finite and compatible. The old source reaches the cap fallback; the new source rejects the nonfinite intermediate. This is consistent with fail-closed intent, but all-finite-input compatibility would be an overly broad claim.",
